WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
Seal a small positive
charge inside a closed box.

2
00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:07.050
Its field passes out through every face.

3
00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:12.510
The total, added over the whole surface,
is the electric flux out of the box.

4
00:00:12.560 --> 00:00:15.340
Now swap the box for a
sphere, a bigger box,

5
00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.190
or a lumpy bag.

6
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:21.240
Every time, the total flux
out is exactly the same.

7
00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:25.640
Why should a lumpy bag let out
exactly as much as a neat sphere?

8
00:00:25.690 --> 00:00:30.140
In this mission, you'll define electric
flux through a flat surface in a uniform

9
00:00:30.190 --> 00:00:31.150
field.

10
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.640
Then you'll add flux over
curved and closed surfaces,

11
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:36.610
and meet Gauss's law.

12
00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:41.560
Your mission: explain why the total
flux out of the box never changes.
